:36},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","03.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","03.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":264,"path":265,"stem":266,"icon":267},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","03.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":269,"title":236,"body":270,"description":1242,"extension":1243,"links":1244,"meta":1245,"navigation":1246,"path":237,"seo":1247,"stem":238,"__hash__":1248},"docs\u002F03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":271,"value":272,"toc":1225},"minimark",[273,277,281,285,296,303,307,317,323,327,332,335,374,378,385,392,398,402,409,464,470,480,493,557,560,628,631,635,638,644,648,651,657,661,664,670,674,681,921,925,931,1132,1136,1221],[274,275,31],"h2",{"id":276},"overview",[278,279,280],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[274,282,284],{"id":283},"format","Format",[286,287,292],"pre",{"className":288,"code":290,"language":291},[289],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[293,294,290],"code",{"__ignoreMap":295},"",[278,297,298,299,302],{},"Everything in brackets (",[293,300,301],{},"[]",") is optional.",[274,304,306],{"id":305},"case","Case",[278,308,309,310,313,314,316],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[293,311,312],{},"OrderService"," and ",[293,315,312],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[286,318,321],{"className":319,"code":320,"language":291},[289],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[293,322,320],{"__ignoreMap":295},[274,324,326],{"id":325},"components","Components",[328,329,331],"h3",{"id":330},"scheme","Scheme",[278,333,334],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[336,337,338,350],"table",{},[339,340,341],"thead",{},[342,343,344,347],"tr",{},[345,346,331],"th",{},[345,348,349],{},"Description",[351,352,353,364],"tbody",{},[342,354,355,361],{},[356,357,358],"td",{},[293,359,360],{},"srv",[356,362,363],{},"Published services and their methods",[342,365,366,371],{},[356,367,368],{},[293,369,370],{},"stream",[356,372,373],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[328,375,377],{"id":376},"scope","Scope",[278,379,380,381,384],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[293,382,383],{},"@"," symbol.",[278,386,387,388,391],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[293,389,390],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[286,393,396],{"className":394,"code":395,"language":291},[289],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[293,397,395],{"__ignoreMap":295},[328,399,401],{"id":400},"zone","Zone",[278,403,404,405,408],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[293,406,407],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[336,410,411,419],{},[339,412,413],{},[342,414,415,417],{},[345,416,401],{},[345,418,349],{},[351,420,421,434,444,454],{},[342,422,423,428],{},[356,424,425],{},[293,426,427],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[356,429,430,431,391],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[293,432,433],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[342,435,436,441],{},[356,437,438],{},[293,439,440],{},"app-api",[356,442,443],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[342,445,446,451],{},[356,447,448],{},[293,449,450],{},"management-api",[356,452,453],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[342,455,456,461],{},[356,457,458],{},[293,459,460],{},"system-api",[356,462,463],{},"The system's own services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[278,465,466,467,469],{},"A cluster member outside the platform's servers can host its services in ",[293,468,450],{},", where organizations' users call them through the management server as they call the platform's own; such a service checks the caller's organization itself.",[278,471,472,473,476,477,479],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[293,474,475],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[293,478,460],{}," is rejected.",[278,481,482,483,485,486,489,490,492],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[293,484,433],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[293,487,488],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[293,491,407],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[336,494,495,508],{},[339,496,497],{},[342,498,499,502,505],{},[345,500,501],{},"Participant",[345,503,504],{},"May send to",[345,506,507],{},"May subscribe to",[351,509,510,526,545],{},[342,511,512,515,523],{},[356,513,514],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[356,516,517,519,520],{},[293,518,440],{},", ",[293,521,522],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[356,524,525],{},"reply destinations only",[342,527,528,531,540],{},[356,529,530],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[356,532,533,519,535,519,537],{},[293,534,450],{},[293,536,440],{},[293,538,539],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[356,541,542,544],{},[293,543,539],{}," — its applications' zones",[342,546,547,550,553],{},[356,548,549],{},"SYSTEM",[356,551,552],{},"everything",[356,554,555],{},[293,556,460],{},[278,558,559],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[336,561,562,575],{},[339,563,564],{},[342,565,566,569,572],{},[345,567,568],{},"Server",[345,570,571],{},"Hosts",[345,573,574],{},"Reaches",[351,576,577,594,611],{},[342,578,579,582,586],{},[356,580,581],{},"org",[356,583,584],{},[293,585,450],{},[356,587,588,519,590,519,592],{},[293,589,450],{},[293,591,460],{},[293,593,440],{},[342,595,596,599,605],{},[356,597,598],{},"system",[356,600,601,519,603],{},[293,602,460],{},[293,604,450],{},[356,606,607,519,609],{},[293,608,460],{},[293,610,450],{},[342,612,613,615,622],{},[356,614,475],{},[356,616,617,519,619],{},[293,618,440],{},[293,620,621],{},"app.*",[356,623,624,519,626],{},[293,625,440],{},[293,627,621],{},[278,629,630],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[328,632,634],{"id":633},"resource-name","Resource Name",[278,636,637],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[286,639,642],{"className":640,"code":641,"language":291},[289],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[293,643,641],{"__ignoreMap":295},[328,645,647],{"id":646},"path","Path",[278,649,650],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[286,652,655],{"className":653,"code":654,"language":291},[289],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[293,656,654],{"__ignoreMap":295},[328,658,660],{"id":659},"version","Version",[278,662,663],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[286,665,668],{"className":666,"code":667,"language":291},[289],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById#1.0.0\nsrv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService#2.0.0\n",[293,669,667],{"__ignoreMap":295},[274,671,673],{"id":672},"factory-function","Factory Function",[278,675,676,677,680],{},"The ",[293,678,679],{},"createCRI"," function provides several overloads for constructing CRI instances:",[286,682,686],{"className":683,"code":684,"language":685,"meta":295,"style":295},"language-typescript shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme mate